# Copy this file to .reviewer-model at your workspace root — beside the
# governing AGENTS.md, not inside a repository — and uncomment
# exactly one command line (or write your own). The implementing agent runs
# that line verbatim after substituting {packet} (review packet file),
# {report} (report output file), and {root} (repository root). The line
# must contain the tool, model, and effort you want — the agent will not
# choose or change them. Never put secrets or API keys in this file; the
# reviewer's stored CLI authentication is used.

# Codex reviewer (replace MODEL, EFFORT, and MCP_OVERRIDES):
# --ignore-user-config keeps MCP servers defined in your user config out
# of the review; authentication still uses the stored login. If your model
# provider is defined in user config, drop --ignore-user-config and treat
# your user-config servers like project-config servers below.
# --disable apps/plugins removes app- and plugin-provided integrations.
# Do not add mcp_servers overrides for app/plugin-provided servers:
# shadowing their registration without its transport breaks config load.
# MCP_OVERRIDES covers only servers defined in config files (the target
# repository's .codex/config.toml, system, or managed configuration).
# From the target repository, inspect `codex mcp list --json`, identify
# those config-file servers, and replace MCP_OVERRIDES with one -c
# argument disabling each by its exact name, for example:
# -c 'mcp_servers={"server.with-dots"={enabled=false},"another"={enabled=false}}'
# If no config-file servers exist, remove MCP_OVERRIDES. An empty
# mcp_servers={} merges with existing settings; it does not clear servers.
# Before running the review, read back `codex mcp list --json` and
# `codex features list` from the target repository with the same -c and
# --disable options: no config-file MCP server may be enabled, and apps,
# plugins, hooks, and multi_agent must all be false. If a remaining enabled
# server cannot be disabled without breaking config load, stop.
# --ignore-rules also prevents inherited execution rules from permitting
# shell commands outside the read-only sandbox.
# codex exec --ephemeral --ignore-rules --ignore-user-config --sandbox read-only --disable apps --disable plugins --disable hooks --disable multi_agent MCP_OVERRIDES -c 'approval_policy="never"' -m MODEL -c 'model_reasoning_effort="EFFORT"' -C {root} - < {packet} > {report}

# Claude reviewer (replace MODEL and EFFORT):
# claude --print --model MODEL --effort EFFORT --safe-mode --tools "Read,Glob,Grep" --allowedTools "Read,Glob,Grep" --disallowedTools "mcp__*" --permission-mode dontAsk --strict-mcp-config --mcp-config '{"mcpServers":{}}' < {packet} > {report}

# Muse reviewer (replace MODEL and EFFORT; add your read-only
# permission/workspace restrictions):
# muse exec --model MODEL --reasoning-effort EFFORT --prompt-file {packet} > {report}
